{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779061007,"nonce":"wnzB7y7H+3HU0m/V8xwQcaWtJJw=","title":"Phase 4: Studio workspace/pipeline vertical slice","message":"## Parent / coordination\n- Roadmap: `fa3978f` — Feedbax/Mandible MVP integration roadmap, Phase 4.\n- Pipeline spec: `0c46f69`.\n- Structural authoring spec: `5378a5d`.\n- Bottom-pane collection issue: `4e0d925`.\n- Manifest/provider contract: `c6c6da0`.\n\n## Problem\nFeedbax now has the first provider/manifest substrate and an execution-contract layer, but Studio still has no durable pipeline/scenario workspace model. Current Studio state is split across `GraphProject`, `analysis_pages`, global training/task/loss stores, one selected training run, and evals under that selected run. That makes visible Studio state diverge from durable specs/manifests and blocks the product-level vertical path described by the roadmap.\n\n## Scope\nBuild the first additive Studio foundation for the Phase 4 vertical slice without hobbling the fuller product that will be built later.\n\nThe first slice should:\n- Add a versioned workspace/pipeline spec with train/eval/analysis/report stages, collection refs, scenario refs, manifest refs, validation state, and UI state.\n- Add a minimal `ScenarioSpec` wrapper around current graph/task/loss/probe/temporal state, preserving room for later biomechanics, objective, selector, report, and visual authoring features.\n- Persist the workspace/scenario model in project save/load while keeping existing project fields available during migration.\n- Move the training panel and run/eval selection toward active-stage state, using existing UI components as temporary editors rather than creating a parallel final UX.\n- Route at least one local Studio execution path through the provider/execution contract where feasible, or add the adapter boundary and tests if full UI execution is too large for this slice.\n- Emit or link manifest refs so later Mandible ingest can see the Studio-produced lineage.\n\n## Non-goals\n- No full Studio redesign in this branch.\n- No irreversible narrowing of the workspace model to only training.\n- No RunPod/Modal live submission here; cloud execution has a contract but live adapters should be separate children.\n- No Mandible UI work in this Feedbax branch.\n- No hidden frontend-only executable semantics introduced as a shortcut.\n\n## Verification\n- Backend model/save-load tests for workspace, stages, scenarios, collection refs, and migration defaults.\n- Frontend type/store tests where available for workspace/stage state.\n- Focused UI smoke or build verification for Studio save/load and active-stage editing.\n- Provider/execution tests if this branch wires execution planning from Studio state.\n\n## Done means\nA saved Studio project can carry an initial durable workspace with pipeline stages and scenario drafts. Existing graph/task/loss/training state can be represented as active-stage/scenario state without losing compatibility with the current UI, and the next agents can extend that foundation into eval, analysis, report, visual objective authoring, cloud execution, and Mandible ingest without replacing this slice.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}